{
	"_comment": "Leaf-row planning and writing vectors, replayed by _shared/lua/test/toml_leaf_rows_vectors_contract.lua on macOS and Linux. entry point: the leaf-row planner turns (source bytes, operations) into batch rows, then the batch writer prepares the candidate bytes from the source (a null source is an absent file). An operation is {path: [segments], value} or {path, delete: true}; a path has at least two segments and no empty one. expect.ok is acceptance of the whole chain (a refusal may come from either step); decoded lists paths of the decoded candidate whose value must equal value, or must be absent when absent is true; contains are substrings of the candidate bytes. Converted from toml_leaf_rows_contract.lua.",
	"entry_point": "leaf-row planner prepare(source, operations) -> rows, then the batch writer's prepare step on (source, rows)",
	"drivers": {
		"macos": "Replays every vector.",
		"linux": "Replays every vector.",
		"windows": "Not ported: one AHK consumer must call the Windows leaf-row planner and batch writer in that order and decode the candidate for the decoded checks."
	},
	"vectors": [
		{
			"id": "bare-leaves-written-as-ordinary-table-rows-in-an-absent-file",
